# Graduate Master's Materials Science Curricular Architecture
#
# Master of Science (M.S.) in Materials Science and Engineering: defect equilibria, microstructural evolution, 2D nanomaterials, and superalloys.

#>spw_cache_univ_masters_mse
#:cache #!materials_science
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the graduate Master of Science (M.S.) curriculum in Materials Science and Engineering, articulating non-stoichiometric defect equilibria, phase-field kinetics, low-dimensional quantum materials, and high-temperature metallurgy."
  ~#degree_culmination: "Graduate Core Examination, Research Proposal, and Master's Thesis Defense"
}

^["advanced_thermodynamics_and_defect_chemistry"]{
  graduate_depth: "Statistical thermodynamics of solids, interfaces, and non-stoichiometry."
  defect_formalisms: #[
    "Kroger-Vink Defect Notation: Fully charged vacancies, interstitials, and anti-site defects in ionic crystals and functional oxides",
    "Brouwer Equilibrium Diagrams: Defect concentration log-log plots as functions of oxygen partial pressure (pO2) and chemical activity",
    "Interfacial Thermodynamics: Surface energy anisotropy, grain boundary segregation isotherms (Langmuir-McLean), and equilibrium crystal shapes via Wulff construction",
    "CALPHAD Computational Thermodynamics: Calculation of phase diagrams from compound energy formalisms and sublattice Gibbs energy models"
  ]
}

^["advanced_phase_transformations_and_microstructural_dynamics"]{
  graduate_core: "Continuum field theories of microstructural evolution."
  transformation_models: .{
    interphase_boundary_structures: #[
      "Coherent interfaces, semi-coherent interfaces with misfit dislocations (Frank-van der Merwe and Matthews-Blakeslee critical thickness limits), and incoherent boundaries",
      "Displacive transformations: Crystallographic Theory of Martensite (PTMC), invariant plane strain, and habit plane prediction"
    ]
    phase_field_formulations: #[
      "Cahn-Hilliard Equation: Nonlinear fourth-order partial differential equation modeling conserved concentration field evolution during spinodal decomposition",
      "Allen-Cahn Equation: Second-order reaction-diffusion equation governing non-conserved structural order parameter field evolution during grain growth",
      "Coarsening Kinetics: Lifshitz-Slyozov-Wagner (LSW) theory of diffusion-controlled Ostwald ripening (mean particle radius scaling as t^(1/3))"
    ]
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["advanced_solid_state_physics_of_materials"]{
  graduate_physics: "Quantum mechanics of electrons and phonons in crystalline lattices."
  condensed_matter_topics: #[
    "Electronic Band Structures & Density of States: First Brillouin zone geometries, van Hove singularities, and tight-binding matrix Hamiltonians",
    "Phonon Dynamics & Thermal Transport: Dynamic matrix diagonalization, acoustic/optical dispersion curves, Umklapp phonon-phonon scattering, and lattice thermal conductivity",
    "Strongly Correlated Systems: Mott insulators, Hubbard model U/W competition, colossal magnetoresistance, and unconventional cuprate/pnictide superconductivity",
    "Multiferroic & Spintronic Materials: Magnetoelectric coupling, spin-orbit torque, magnetic skyrmions, and giant magnetoresistance (GMR) in magnetic multilayers"
  ]
}

^["low_dimensional_nanomaterials_and_heterostructures"]{
  materials_frontiers: "Synthesis, physics, and device integration of nanoscale systems."
  quantum_structures: .{
    quantum_confinement: "Density of states transition from 3D bulk continuous square-root to 2D stepped, 1D peaked, and 0D discrete delta-function levels"
    two_dimensional_crystals: #[
      "Graphene: Dirac cones, linear dispersion, massless Dirac fermions, and ballistic electronic transport",
      "Transition Metal Dichalcogenides (TMDs): MoS2 and WSe2 direct bandgap transitions in monolayers, valleytronics, and circular dichroism",
      "Moiré Superlattices & Twistronics: Flat band formation in magic-angle twisted bilayer graphene (1.1 degrees) yielding correlated insulating and superconducting states"
    ]
    epitaxial_synthesis: "Atomic Layer Deposition (ALD), Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD), and ultra-high-vacuum Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE)"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["advanced_polymers_and_soft_matter_physics"]{
  graduate_macromolecular: #[
    "Polymer Conformation Statistics: Gaussian chain, self-avoiding walk with Flory exponent (nu = 3/5), and radius of gyration Rg scaling",
    "Flory-Huggins Solution Theory: Lattice model, interaction parameter chi, spinodal/binodal phase curves, and upper/lower critical solution temperatures",
    "Reptation Dynamics: De Gennes tube model for entangled polymer melts, primitive path relaxation, and reptation time scaling with molecular weight cubed (M^3)",
    "Block Copolymer Morphology: Microphase separation into lamellar, cylindrical, bicontinuous gyroid, and spherical domains driven by chi*N product"
  ]
}

^["high_temperature_superalloys_and_extreme_materials"]{
  structural_frontiers: #[
    "Nickel-Based Superalloys: Gamma/gamma-prime (Ni3Al, L1_2) coherent precipitate microstructures, anomalous yield strength peak at 750C, and rafting kinetics",
    "Single-Crystal Solidification: Bridgman-Stockbarger directional solidification furnaces with spiral grain selectors eliminating high-angle grain boundaries in jet turbine blades",
    "High-Entropy Alloys (HEAs): Multi-principal element alloys (Cantor alloy FeNiCrCoMn), four core effects (high entropy, sluggish diffusion, severe lattice distortion, cocktail effect)"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Master's-level materials science is the mastery of thermodynamic and kinetic landscapes: navigating free energy valleys to trap matter into metastable states of astonishing strength and electronic splendor."
  ~#wonder: "Why does rotating two sheets of graphene by exactly 1.1 degrees transform a semi-metal into an unconventional superconductor?"

  principles: #[
    "Metastability is a superpower: The most valuable engineering materials (martensitic steel, diamond, bulk metallic glasses) are thermodynamically unstable states preserved by frozen kinetics.",
    "Order parameter rigor: Whether modeling a grain boundary, a ferromagnetic domain, or a polymer blend, continuous field variables capture physics that discrete atomistic models miss.",
    "Multi-scale coherence: A master's thesis must connect sub-nanometer atomic bonding to millimeter-scale macroscopic mechanical failure."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Phase-field simulations must satisfy thermodynamic consistency (monotonically decreasing total free energy functional over time).",
  "Reported epitaxial thin-film structures must declare film thickness, substrate lattice mismatch, and misfit strain relaxation mechanisms.",
  "Master's thesis defense requires demonstration of both physical synthesis/characterization competency and computational/analytical modeling.",
}

#>wonder_masters_mse_1
?["How does high-entropy alloy (HEA) sluggish diffusion suppress vacancy-assisted creep deformation at temperatures exceeding 0.8 homologous melting point?"]{
  #:depth #!physical ~#lens(athermal_diffusion_barriers)
  ~#hypothesis: "Severely distorted chemical environments in five-element equiatomic HEAs create rugged atomic energy landscapes where vacancy migration activation enthalpies vary wildly, trapping vacancies in local energy wells and reducing secondary creep rates by two orders of magnitude compared to traditional nickel superalloys."
  !probe{ "Measure steady-state creep strain rates and vacancy migration barriers using high-temperature synchrotron X-ray diffraction and positron annihilation lifetime spectroscopy." }
  $%[creep.steady_state_strain_rate, defects.vacancy_migration_activation_ev]
}
